---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { PROMPTS } from "../../data/docs";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Prompts and resources"
  description="Ready-made tasks NexQL offers your app, often as slash commands, and the database objects it exposes as resources."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Guide · 07</p>
    <h1>Prompts and resources</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Besides tools, NexQL offers your app a set of ready-made tasks (MCP prompts) and a way to attach a table's description to
      a conversation (MCP resources). How they appear depends on the app: often as slash commands or an attach menu.
    </p>

    <h2>Prompts</h2>
    <p>Each one starts a multi-step task with the right tools. Pick it, fill in the blanks, and the assistant takes it from there.</p>
    <div class="prompts">
      {
        PROMPTS.map((p) => (
          <div class="prompt">
            <code class="pname">/{p.name}</code>
            <p>{p.description}</p>
            {p.arguments.length > 0 && (
              <ul>
                {p.arguments.map((a) => (
                  <li>
                    <code>{a.name}</code> {a.description}
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            )}
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <h2>Resources</h2>
    <p>
      Every table, view, materialized view and function in the schema index is available as a resource, addressed like this:
    </p>
    <pre><code>nexql://&#123;connectionId&#125;/&#123;database&#125;/object/&#123;schema&#125;/&#123;name&#125;</code></pre>
    <p>
      Reading one returns a structural card: columns, keys, indexes and, for views and functions, the definition. Attaching{" "}
      <code>nexql://prod/shop/object/public/orders</code> to a conversation is a quick way to say “this table” without the
      assistant having to search for it.
    </p>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .prompts {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .prompt {
    padding: 16px 18px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--panel);
  }
  .pname {
    font-size: 15px !important;
    color: var(--accent);
    background: none !important;
    border: 0 !important;
    padding: 0 !important;
  }
  .prompt p {
    margin-top: 6px;
  }
  .prompt ul {
    margin-top: 8px;
    font-size: 14.5px;
  }
</style>
